ASSISTANT To configure a local **llm-lite** server that supports dispatching requests to **OpenRouter** models, you'll need to:
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 1. **Set up `llm-lite`** (if not already present in your repo).
ASSISTANT    - Follow the same module pattern as `llm-netogallo` (see `llm-netogallo/config.nix` and `llm-netogallo/setup.nix`).
ASSISTANT    - Create a new directory `llm-lite/` with similar structure.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 2. **Configure OpenRouter API Access**
ASSISTANT    - Ensure you have an **OpenRouter API key** (set as an environment variable, e.g., `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`).
ASSISTANT    - In your `llm-lite/config.nix`, define the OpenRouter endpoint and authentication.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 3. **Dispatch Logic**
ASSISTANT    - Modify the server logic (likely in `setup.nix` or a new file) to:
ASSISTANT      - Accept incoming requests.
ASSISTANT      - Forward them to OpenRouter’s API (`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`).
ASSISTANT      - Handle responses/errors.
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT 4. **Integrate with Your Flake**
ASSISTANT    - Update `flake.nix` to include the new `llm-lite` module (similar to how `llm-netogallo` is included).
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ### Example Structure (Based on `llm-netogallo`):
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT # llm-lite/config.nix
ASSISTANT { lib, ... }:
ASSISTANT {
ASSISTANT   openrouter.apiKey = lib.mkOption {
ASSISTANT     type = lib.types.str;
ASSISTANT     default = "";
ASSISTANT     description = "OpenRouter API key";
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT   openrouter.endpoint = lib.mkOption {
ASSISTANT     type = lib.types.str;
ASSISTANT     default = "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions";
ASSISTANT     description = "OpenRouter API endpoint";
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT }
ASSISTANT ```
ASSISTANT 
ASSISTANT ```nix
ASSISTANT # llm-lite/setup.nix
ASSISTANT { config, ... }:
ASSISTANT {
ASSISTANT   # Logic to start a local server that proxies to OpenRouter
ASSISTANT   systemd.services.llm-lite = {
ASSISTANT     serviceConfig.ExecStart = ''
ASSISTANT       llm-lite-server --openrouter-key "${config.openrouter.apiKey}"
ASSISTANT     '';
ASSISTANT   };
ASSISTANT }
ASSISTANT ```
